        <body>
            <div xml:id="d676">

                <pb facs="0821" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/460</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic">February 18,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received February 26.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 753</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that I have
                    brought the Department’s telegram of February the 11th to the attention of
                    President Menocal, who assures me that no effort will be made to pass the <pb
                        facs="0822" n="698" xml:id="pg698"/> new budget requiring about $104,000,000
                    to run the Cuban Government, but that it will function for the coming fiscal
                    year under the 1918–1919 budget.</p>
                <p>More detailed information regarding the proposed new budget is to be furnished me
                    in the near future.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Boaz W. Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
